# Tool rules

- Never use heredocs in tool or shell commands. Write files with the agent's
  file tools and verify after patching.
- Search with `rg`, not `grep`.
- Run commands through `execute_javascript` (`tools.call("shell", ...)`), not
  a raw shell tool, for the parent session and all subagents.

# Long-running commands

- Never start a build, benchmark, fuzz run or gate in the background and poll
  it. Run it once, in the foreground, with `timeout_secs` set to a realistic
  upper bound (up to 3600), and redirect output to a log.
- Read the log tail once when the call returns. Do not re-run a multi-minute
  command just to check progress; make it emit timestamped `phase=` lines and
  inspect those instead.
- If a command can take more than about two minutes, run it in the parent
  session rather than delegating it, and cap repetitions/iterations unless the
  task explicitly needs more.
- Give every subagent a wall-clock budget, the exact command(s) to run, and
  the minimum `max_turns` that can finish the task. Ask for `tail`/`rg`-sized
  summaries, not full logs.
